+EIGHTMAX TEST WORKBENCH 0.30.0 — PRECOMPUTED STRATEGY LIBRARY (NOT VERSION 1.0)
+
+QUICK START — unchanged: extract the entire ZIP, double-click START-DESKTOP.cmd (or open START.html in Edge/Chrome).
+TO CHECK THIS PC: close any running desktop host, then double-click RUN-RELEASE-ACCEPTANCE.cmd and send the ZIP it puts on your Desktop.
+
+WHAT IS NEW, STATED PLAINLY
+- STRATEGY LIBRARY: trained postflop strategies are stored once on disk and reused by every table and hand that reaches the exact
+  same situation. Simulated tables now LOOK UP strategies instead of training while a table waits ("Decision Mode").
+  Dashboard: "Strategy library" (left menu). One-click files: RECORD-SITUATIONS.cmd (play simulated hands and note which situations
+  had no strategy), PRECOMPUTE-STRATEGIES.cmd (train those situations), VERIFY-STRATEGIES.cmd, EXPORT-STRATEGIES.cmd,
+  IMPORT-STRATEGIES.cmd, CANCEL-TRAINING.cmd. Library folder: %LOCALAPPDATA%\EightMax-Test-Workbench\StrategyLibrary.
+- When no strategy exists the program says: "No trained strategy is available for this situation. Add it to the training queue."
+  It never invents probabilities. Simulations then use the clearly labelled scripted test policy.
+- MEASURED (Linux development machine, 4 CPUs, simulated tables, same seeded hands as 0.29's benchmark D):
+  worst-table P95 decision cycle at 10 tables: 0.29 = 1,557 ms (re-run here); 0.30 with the needed strategies in the library =
+  221 ms (read from disk) / 244 ms (pre-loaded); 0.30 still training inside the decision path ("Study Mode") = 432 ms.
+  Strategy lookup itself: about 0.5 ms from memory, 3-11 ms from disk in-thread.
+- NOT SOLVED: on NEW hands the library rarely has the exact postflop situation (2 of 86 postflop decisions in a 10-table run on
+  unseen hands, with a partial flop catalogue). Exact boards and stacks vary too much; precomputation must run for a long time
+  (your i7-13700F is much faster than the development machine) and still cannot cover every turn and river.
+- ACCURACY: exact exploitability is now measured on small reference games with independent code. The solver converges
+  (0.08 bb at 200,000 updates on a reference river game) but strategies actually stored by the default settings were about
+  20 % of the pot exploitable on heads-up rivers. Coverage is not accuracy. Nothing is GTO-certified.
+- WINDOWS: the 0.29 executables ran in Windows CI; 0.30 rebuilt the host, capture tool and WGC helper (new version number and the
+  library route). desktop\COMPONENT-VERSIONS.json is now generated from evidence and says exactly which files ran where.
+  Nothing has run on your PC yet. No external poker client was chosen, inspected or integrated. FFmpeg is still not bundled.
+
+NEW IN 0.30.0: docs/STRATEGY-LIBRARY.md, docs/0.30-validation-report.md (final report), docs/CHANGELOG.md, reports/0.30-*, evidence/.
+
+---- previous release notes follow ----
+
